# Settings restored at the next start of a d435i-ioc instance.
#
# Macros: P (record prefix, e.g. RS405: or RS435:)
#
# Two groups, both of which otherwise reset on every IOC restart:
#
#  1. Camera configuration. RSStreamMode is the one that bites -- the driver
#     defaults to 640x480 @ 30fps, so a site that runs at 15fps silently goes
#     back to 30 (and to twice the USB isochronous load) after any restart.
#
#  2. Viewer plugin wiring. These come up disabled, and a viewer that was
#     already running does not re-send its startup writes to the new IOC --
#     the panes then show the single value fetched at connect and never
#     update again, which reads as a broken camera rather than a disabled
#     plugin.

# ---- Acquisition ----
$(P)cam1:ImageMode
$(P)cam1:NumImages

# ---- Stream configuration ----
$(P)cam1:RSStreamMode

# ---- Sensor options ----
$(P)cam1:RSExposure
$(P)cam1:RSGain
$(P)cam1:RSAutoExposure
$(P)cam1:RSLaserPower
$(P)cam1:RSEmitterEnabled

# ---- Post-processing filters ----
$(P)cam1:RSDecimationEnable
$(P)cam1:RSDecimationMag
$(P)cam1:RSSpatialEnable
$(P)cam1:RSSpatialAlpha
$(P)cam1:RSSpatialDelta
$(P)cam1:RSSpatialMag
$(P)cam1:RSTemporalEnable
$(P)cam1:RSTemporalAlpha
$(P)cam1:RSTemporalDelta
$(P)cam1:RSHoleFillEnable
$(P)cam1:RSHoleFillMode

# ---- Alignment / pointcloud ----
$(P)cam1:RSAlignEnable
$(P)cam1:RSPointCloudEnable

# ---- Viewer plugin chain ----
# Colour is RGB8 interleaved, which PyDMImageView cannot draw directly, so the
# dual-view screen routes image1 through the colour-convert plugin as Mono.
$(P)CC1:ColorModeOut
$(P)CC1:EnableCallbacks
$(P)image1:NDArrayPort
$(P)image1:EnableCallbacks
$(P)image2:EnableCallbacks
